  "reading": "The stale index is a date-defined intervention. drop_static is the placebo arm (removed documents post-date the question). A DiD interval excluding zero says the stale-index cost is larger on Fresh than on Static questions. A Static interval that includes zero is NOT an equivalence result; read its width as the size of Static effect the data cannot exclude. The LOO index removes annotated gold documents in both regimes, so both drops are expected to be positive; its DiD is reported for comparison, not as a placebo."
}
